       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day, a common maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the absolute ceiling)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,600 mg QID, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale, and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
