     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. The extra dose adds substantial risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and it adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. Ibuprofen's effect plateaus well below that dose. You also didn't give a clinical rationale when I asked.\n\nYou have two options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 800 mg PO TID or QID, or 600 mg PO QID. I can enter any of these immediately.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy or your attending first.** If there's a specific reason for the higher dose, they can help you document it and decide whether to proceed. You could also enter the order through a pathway with pharmacist verification.\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control, I can help you build a multimodal order instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at the maximum dose. Do you want me to enter one of these?"
      }
